defect and the splice specializes to one.","The pair core certificate retains the exact condition nuP(U_j)=1; the selected handle exists."],"references":["GQ2.Dyadic.eval_pro2_tameSplice","GQ2.Dyadic.tameSpecializes_tameSplice","GQ2.Dyadic.Instances.EvenMHeadHandlePairSpliceSupply.flexibleCore_headHandlePairSplice","GQ2.Dyadic.Instances.EvenMHeadHandlePairSpliceSupply.headHandlePairSpliceW_specializes"],"title":"Tame and pro-two specialization reductions"},{"number":3,"paragraphs":["All three profiles use a finite base group C and finite exponent-two coefficient module A. These are identities on all cochains, not just cycles. Columns not displayed vanish. The resolver is pinned at 4 times the finite base-group exponent and is valid at WordLift level.","Scalar: every generator action is trivial. Unramified: finite exponent-two coefficients, wild and tau actions trivial, sigma fixed-point-free with trivial two-primary action, and death of the actual pinned changed-word family. Ramified: explicit finite surjective head projection with compatible action, wild head one, actual tame relation, and tau fixed-point-free with trivial two-primary action. No raw-word death or commuting sigma/tau premise is inserted."],"references":["GQ2.Dyadic.Instances.TameSpliceScalarFoxNormal.pairSplice_scalar_rows","GQ2.Dyadic.Instances.TameSpliceUnramifiedFoxRows.pairSplice_unramified_rows","GQ2.Dyadic.Instances.TameSpliceRamifiedFoxNormal.tameSplice_ramified_rows","GQ2.Dyadic.GeneralFoxTemplate.scalar_pair_input","GQ2.Dyadic.GeneralFoxTemplate.unramified_pair_input","GQ2.Dyadic.GeneralFoxTemplate.ramified_pair_input"],"title":"Evaluated Fox Jacobian"},{"number":4,"paragraphs":["The following lists are exported from the same typed profile as the input and target rows. Their denotations are definitionally the lists in the original FoxCertificate records. Every scale carries a formal inverse; the actual records prove both inverse products.","In each nonscalar sector k is the half-period of the actual coefficient action, so its odd order is 2k+1. It is not the handle rank, not an assumed ambient group order, and not a fixed source parameter. q is the source residue size. Composition applies the inner operator first."],"references":["GQ2.Dyadic.GeneralFoxTemplate.scalar_pair_signature","GQ2.Dyadic.GeneralFoxTemplate.unramified_pair_signature","GQ2.Dyadic.GeneralFoxTemplate.ramified_pair_signature"],"title":"Ordered invertible operations and carried inverses"},{"number":5,"paragraphs":["Replay of the preceding invertible lists gives these literal identity-pivot targets on all cochains. The scalar second row is zero. The ramified sigma pivot is obtained after the displayed column shear; it must not be read as an identity for the unsheared input."],"references":["GQ2.Dyadic.GeneralFoxTemplate.scalar_pair_signature","GQ2.Dyadic.GeneralFoxTemplate.unramified_pair_signature","GQ2.Dyadic.GeneralFoxTemplate.ramified_pair_signature"],"title":"Reduced normal matrices"},{"number":6,"paragraphs":["The actual word supplies a single coefficient-independent UniformStokesSupply. It includes pinned resolution, endpoint and full Stokes duality for every finite elementary coefficient module pushed from the actual source. The simple-action profiles feed the proved composition-series exact-diagram extension; checking dimensions only on simple modules is not substituted for that argument. The statement is uniform in all source parameters and h."],"references":["GQ2.Dyadic.Instances.EvenMHeadHandlePairSpliceSupply.uniformStokesSupply_headHandlePairSplice"],"title":"Stokes chain identity and all coefficients"},{"number":7,"paragraphs":["The exported quadratic expression below is the full endpoint phase. Here q_0 is the coefficient quadratic form and B=polar(q_0), distinct from the residue size q in the Fox rows. It is not inferred from its polar matrix. The unramified comparison retains the factor-set charge until its proved faithful-head vanishing; the ramified splice retains the complete extraspecial evaluation and then uses the existing head swap. This is not a claim that the raw ramified expression equals the displayed form before changing coordinates."],"references":["GQ2.Dyadic.hessEvalZ_tameSplice_ramified","GQ2.Dyadic.GeneralPhaseTemplate.denote_compactPhase","GQ2.Dyadic.GeneralPhaseTemplate.sourcePhase_eq_denote","GQ2.Dyadic.Instances.EvenMHeadHandlePairProjectedPhase.QZero_headHandlePairSplice_unramified_compactPhase"],"title":"Full extraspecial Hessian"},{"number":8,"paragraphs":["The original source comparison map is proved additive, then upgraded to an F2-linear equivalence with exactly the same forward and inverse functions. Its domain is the actual source cocycle quotient. The original Hessian record proves QZeroBar(x)=Q(cov(x)), and the two inverse equations. The matrices below are relative to the coefficient pairing B; B itself is not declared to be the identity matrix."],"references":["GQ2.Dyadic.Instances.WordPhaseCompactCertificates.sourceCompactHessianOfComparison_cov_apply","GQ2.Dyadic.GeneralPhaseTemplate.sourceHessian_cov_eq_denote","GQ2.Dyadic.GeneralPhaseTemplate.polar_denote_compactPhase","GQ2.Dyadic.Instances.WordPhasePolarNormal.reducedCoefficientMatrix_mul_inverse","GQ2.Dyadic.Instances.TameSpliceBoundaryHessianCertificates.pairBoundaryHessian"],"title":"Linear normal coordinates and polar inverse"},{"number":9,"paragraphs":["The original Hessian record contains the original PhaseCoverCertificate. For |V|=2^d, its base dimension is (h+1)d and its base sign is +1. The diagonal and cross embeddings put v into the first and second head slots respectively and zero in every other slot. It proves the full diagonal identity Q(j0(v))=dat.f(v,v), the cross-polar identity, the endpoint cardinality and the signed Gauss sum.","At every relevant actual boundary lift, the named boundary producer derives the projected head hypotheses internally and returns this original record. The downstream affine determinant remains a theorem for every required cover and character, not just an unshifted Gauss value."],"references":["GQ2.Dyadic.Instances.WordPhaseCompactCertificates.compactPhaseCover","GQ2.Dyadic.GeneralPhaseTemplate.compactPhaseCover_tree","GQ2.Dyadic.GeneralPhaseCoverTemplate.compactTemplate_agrees","GQ2.Dyadic.Instances.TameSpliceBoundaryHessianCertificates.pairBoundaryHessian","GQ2.Dyadic.Instances.EvenMHeadHandlePairSpliceBoundary.headHandlePairSplice_determinant"],"title":"Original affine phase-cover record"},{"number":10,"paragraphs":["The word, Fox, phase and phase-cover hashes identify symbolic templates. They do not hash actual q, nuP, eta, shear, correction, coefficient-space or action-period values. Uniform Lean denotation and certificate-signature bridges bind their semantic uses. This combined packet additionally binds the generated section content and direct source bytes.","Strong checking re-emits all four Lean exports and checks every cited declaration's existence and standard-three axiom footprint, and compares the printed type transcript on replay. It does not assert independently authored expected signatures. The probe imports existing olean artifacts; direct source hashes alone do not prove that those bytes produced those artifacts or came from an atomic filesystem snapshot. A separate isolated build is required. External dependency artifacts are reused. Prose remains an editorial exposition of the checked objects. This STAGED packet does not approve the changed source selection, replace the frozen five-fixture manifest, activate a merge gate, or certify the original frozen-M theorem."],"references":[],"title":"Same-tree hashes, replay and trust boundary"}],"source_provenance":{"scope":"direct-sources-only-not-transitive-build-provenance","sha256":{"GQ2/Dyadic/Instances/TameSpliceBoundaryHessianCertificates.lean":"6b8cfc4a3128ee0c31382b1e3c97bded9b6acb3ea757ac3b9266a24d06a9a3a7","GQ2/Dyadic/Instances/TameSpliceFoxCertificates.lean":"67a7418db74c6a1d26848000e8daa